  "published": "2026-08-27T10:06:46.85Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.0.18\n- Reads a project without re-proving the same file once per citation: a health check over 1,600 facts and 200 records drops from 28 seconds to about one. Batches are proved once per build, citations are read as one set, change lineage is checked against changes already in hand, and file stamps are compared once per build.\n- Projections read the collection once instead of listing every record and then reading each again; collection reads parse in parallel and from bytes, with compile-time serializer metadata.\n- The portal's read cache no longer stamps `.git` or archived document history.\n- A configuration written by 0.0.10 opens again: the retired `trust` block and the earlier lifecycle profile id are read past and rewritten on the next write.\n\n0.0.17\n- Adds a delivery order for epics: `knowledge order set <nde_id> --position <n>` puts an epic where the project means it to come, and the board reads in that order. It gates nothing.\n- Shows every role what it may do to a need, a requirement, a component, a story and a change, keyed to the same badge the board draws.\n- Tags a board row once, beside its title, instead of putting the tag in a different column for every kind and twice on a task.\n- Makes the platforms screen read-only; adding or removing a platform stays a coordinator's move with `lifecycle platform add`.\n- Explains a refusal properly: every reason is shown, not only the ones naming an observation, and every id in it opens the record it names.\n- Reworks the portal's motion, press feedback, reduced-motion/transparency/contrast handling, and the document reading surface; fixes a project menu clipped inside the rail.",
